 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "slate",
   "title": "Step 0 · Contracts and schemas: what each side must send and return",
   "items": [
    "contracts/dps-jobs-api.yaml:32 POST /dps/v1/jobs, :99 GET /jobs/{id}/result, :333 GET /events: every call Spring makes",
    "Caller schema contracts/schemas/job-request.json: jobType, document (objectKey, sha256, fileName, mediaType, sizeBytes), context (:91 tenant, CP, borrower, facility IDs, expectedType)",
    "Same rules in Python: dps/src/dps/api/jobs.py:114 JobRequest, :67 DocumentRef, :93 JobContext (pydantic rejects unknown or missing fields)",
    "Page model schema contracts/schemas/page-model.json: what extraction produces (pages, text, line boxes, tables)",
    "Skill answer schema dps/src/dps/skills/covenants/schema.json: the exact JSON the agent must return (name, value, page, quote)",
    "Extraction (result) schema contracts/schemas/result.json:82 field: value, source page + quote + box, method, confidence, issues, status"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Step 1 · Spring sends the job (dps/src/dps/api/jobs.py)",
   "items": [
    "The RM uploads in CTS; Spring stores the file in the DMS and calls POST /dps/v1/jobs",
    ":312 submit_job receives it; :166 validate_job checks the job type is allowed and the file format is supported",
    "validate_job opens the stored file and recomputes its SHA-256; if it differs from what Spring sent, the job is refused",
    ":268 _input_key = document + context + pipeline version; if a job with that key exists, DPS returns it (duplicate: true) = 'extraction in progress'",
    ":240 create_job inserts dps_job (status QUEUED) and dps_document, and writes event dps.job.accepted (dps/src/dps/feed.py:39) in the same transaction",
    "DPS answers 202 Accepted with the jobId at once; no reading happens in the API"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Step 2 · Queue and Python worker (dps/src/dps/jobs.py, worker.py)",
   "items": [
    "worker.py:131 run_once: the worker asks the dps_job table for work; when empty it sleeps 2 seconds",
    "jobs.py:85 claim: one UPDATE 'set RUNNING, owned by me, only if still QUEUED' (compare-and-set), so two workers never take one job",
    "jobs.py:162 renew_lease: heartbeat keeps locked_until alive; a dead worker's lease expires and another worker takes the job",
